  "note": "Annual retirement of two councillors in each of the five wards of Londonderry Corporation, with a third West Ward seat vacant through the death of Michael M'Menamin; nominations Friday 5 January 1934. All eleven nominees, five Nationalists and six Unionists, were returned unopposed and there was no poll (Derry Journal, 8 January 1934). No party labels are printed against the names. John Doherty replaced J. T. Towers, who did not seek re-election; John Francis Doherty filled the vacancy left by the death of Michael M'Menamin. Returned unopposed."
